WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.000
- You have some baby news, congrats!

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.395
- Yes, thank you!

00:00:03.395 --> 00:00:05.843
- [Kelly] Yes, it's exciting.

00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:09.280
- This is another big
addition to the family.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.660
A lot of people may or may not know

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.470
that I had issues getting pregnant,

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.890
you know, when me and
my husband got married.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.490
So we had did the IVF treatment,
and we got our son Ace.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.550
He's three now and we wanted
to have another child.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.810
We still had two more embryos from that.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.110
And because I had a high-risk pregnancy

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.010
we were trying to figure out,

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.440
okay, what's the best
way to go about this?

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.760
And we decided to go with a surrogate.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.930
And she decided to help me and my husband.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:35.763
- That's amazing.

00:00:35.763 --> 00:00:39.290
I love it 'cause you're
actually documenting it

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.480
on the show, right?

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.313
This season.
- Yes.

00:00:41.313 --> 00:00:42.310
- And I think that's really important,

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.960
I have many friends that have suffered

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.060
from trying to have children,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.590
trying, trying, and can't do it.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.480
And like, it's a very important thing

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.650
to be confident and comfortable,

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.480
saying like, "Look, my
body, it wasn't made for,"

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.870
my body, by the way, was
not made for pregnancy.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.810
I was hospitalized, it was horrible.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:58.690
- Oh, my goodness.
- God bless surrogates.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.750
- It's a very selfless act.
- My body, also not

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:01.843
made for pregnancy.

00:01:01.843 --> 00:01:04.820
(all laughing)
(audience claps)

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:07.150
- It's a hard, if your
body, if it doesn't take,

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.933
it is like so hard on you.

00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:10.320
So it's an amazing thing.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.680
I think it's so awesome that
you're sharing that, that's a

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:13.513
very personal thing.
- Can I ask a question?

00:01:13.513 --> 00:01:16.657
Will you go into the, will
you be there for the delivery?

00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:17.490
- Yeah!

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.940
For sure, I mean, that's
a lot of what you'll see

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.160
on the show this season.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:23.200
Like, you'll see we're going

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.970
to doctor appointments together,

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:27.050
we're, you know, just that whole process.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:29.840
Because I don't think
anybody actually showed it,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.560
because a lot of people
are quiet about it.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.960
Like, honestly, I really
didn't even tell anybody

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.010
that we were expecting a
child until the show announced

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.620
that it was airing a new season.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.340
Because I didn't really
know how to share that

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.120
with a lot of my friends even.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:43.953
A lot of my friends were like,

00:01:43.953 --> 00:01:45.310
"Wait a minute you're having a baby?"

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.650
You know, it was like
really crazy to them.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:48.580
But at the same time,

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.350
I didn't really wanna hear
anybody else's opinion at first.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:53.100
And so to do it--
You wanna do you.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.410
- Yeah, to do it on the
show it's like a big deal

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:56.930
because it's like, you don't know

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:59.850
how people are going to comment.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.220
Because, you know, the first thing--

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.440
- You're getting a beautiful child,

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.760
who the hell cares what they say?

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.678
- That is true, exactly.
(audience applauds)

00:02:05.678 --> 00:02:06.511
Good point.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:10.120
- And I think that you're, honestly,

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.780
that is a really touchy subject

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.650
with a lot of my friends.
- It is.

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:13.670
- That's like really hard.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.490
Like for a woman, especially,
there's such a sense

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.720
of failure you feel, like
when you can't do it.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.280
So it's really cool that
you're open about it.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.113
- Thank you.

00:02:22.113 --> 00:02:24.150
With my first child,
Riley, it was in my 20s,

00:02:26.008 --> 00:02:27.770
you know, I didn't
really have to try hard.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.300
But then, you know, later in
life when I met my husband,

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.400
I'm thinking that everything

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.440
was just gonna happen, and it didn't.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.460
So I think a lot of women start

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.870
to have that struggle as they get older.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.740
- [Kelly] Yeah, I didn't have
my kids till I was in my 30s.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.568
It was, oh, and I didn't
ever look like that!

00:02:41.568 --> 00:02:42.991
(all laughing)

00:02:42.991 --> 00:02:44.335
Nope, definitely didn't!

